 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The relative pronoun in the nominative",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about who does something (the subject), the relative pronoun is **der** (masculine), **die** (feminine), **das** (neuter) and **die** (plural). Example: **Der Mann, der am Flughafen arbeitet, ist mein Onkel** (the man who works at the airport is my uncle). It always goes between commas.",
      "The conjugated verb of the relative clause goes **at the end**: **arbeitet**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The noun determines the gender",
     "texto": [
      "The relative pronoun agrees with the noun it refers to, that is, with its gender and number. So: **Die Stadt, die schön ist** (the city that is beautiful). **Das Hotel, das neu ist** (the hotel that is new).",
      "Watch out: the relative pronoun isn't always the same as the article, but here in the nominative it almost always matches."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
